{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/flutter/android.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328599Z","id":"b837564b9582bbc4ce446d66c4a0a825a1ae850a403a3f6dbae9f6a39bd326f3","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:apk's android_binary has no proguard_specs, so no R8: against Gradle's app-release.apk (flutter build apk --release, 45 MB) it carries four dex files of 17 MB uncompressed (classes.dex 9.4 MB, classes2 5.0 MB, classes4 2.6 MB) where Gradle's has one of 1.2 MB, Kotlin's commonMain/nativeMain .knm metadata files Gradle drops, no assets/dexopt/baseline.prof, and unobfuscated resource names; the APK is 56 MB. Shrinking was left out because R8 keep rules missing for a reflective use (a plugin's, the embedding's) fail only at run time, and neither APK was run on a device in the change that added the target. Flutter's Gradle plugin applies flutter_proguard_rules.pro and AGP's proguard-android-optimize.txt; the plugins' consumer rules already reach android_binary through rules_flutter.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":234},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"6b2b95a003d72034f41e0af4c5d8b1de1b4ca62d4727ea9a82d22f0f2f36829b"},"suggested_fix":"Pass proguard_specs (Flutter's flutter_proguard_rules.pro, from @flutter_dev_root, plus AGP's optimize defaults) and shrink_resources = 1 to the android_binary in flutter_fat_apk, then install over a Gradle-built APK and exercise every plugin (notifications, location, camera, file picker, share, dictation, WebView).","summary":"The Bazel-built APK is not shrunk with R8 as Gradle's release build is","tags":["revisit:the APK can be tested on a device or emulator in CI","apk","size","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/flutter/android.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:18:09.396513Z","id":"33d82c2ee000b333f5e8cfdbc64abb8c42129e188a2eebdc60deda2aae870e0b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0ecec9bfc","summary":"Done in 0ecec9bfc: R8 with AGP's optimized defaults, Flutter's rules and the libraries' own, shrink_resources, no desugared JDK library. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:apk_test --test_output=all: 'PASS: one dex, shrunk (1236620 bytes)', against Gradle's 1218072-byte classes.dex; the APK is 51.0 MB. Not yet run on a device (see the record on apps/clax_app/BUILD.bazel).","supersedes":"b837564b9582bbc4ce446d66c4a0a825a1ae850a403a3f6dbae9f6a39bd326f3","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/flutter/ios.bzl","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:21:02.471601Z","id":"a04021ee2ca98bbe5a6392889f61ffe6071a29898960598165024b23328b47b7","body":{"detail":"Without :ios_plugin_frameworks, bazelisk build //apps/clax_app:ios_app -c dbg fails at link with undefined _OBJC_CLASS_$_LPLinkMetadata (share_plus's FPPSharePlusPlugin.o; share_plus.podspec: s.ios.weak_framework = 'LinkPresentation') and _kUTTypeGIF, _kUTTypeImage, _kUTTypeMovie (image_picker_ios). The list is kept by hand: a plugin added or upgraded with another such framework fails the same way at link, naming the symbol, not the framework.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":54},"end":{"line":68},"content_hash":"9b1afbaa3c3677cac5f6c4270520af766f7001116bbb6495b55b3c14c82a9b3d"},"suggested_fix":"Add the framework to :ios_plugin_frameworks, or give the plugin an overlay (bazel/flutter/plugin_overlays/<package>/<major>/) passing sdk_frameworks to its flutter_apple_plugin_library; the overlay is per plugin and must carry the Android half too for share_plus.","summary":"The iOS app links LinkPresentation and MobileCoreServices for share_plus and image_picker_ios by hand: rules_flutter's generated plugin libraries link no system framework a plugin's podspec or #import needs","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
